<title>ITALY: Credito H1 net profit falls to 70.5bn lire.</title>
<headline>Credito H1 net profit falls to 70.5bn lire.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			 70.5 vs   90.8</p>
<p>    Parent loss (after extraordinaries) 18.0 vs   33.3 (profit)</p>
<p>    Consolidated net profit		 54.8 vs  104.7</p>
<p>    Provisions				 289.3 vs  136.8</p>
<p>Note: Credito Italiano said in a statement that its performance in the first months of the second half pointed to a full year result which would be appreciably better than in 1995, when it made a net profit of 192.1 billion lire at the parent company level.  </p>
<p>    Interest margins		     1,136.7 vs  1,246.8</p>
<p>    Intermediary margins		 1,729.7 vs  1,510.8</p>
<p>    Client loans		   37,914.1 vs 38,130.2 (end Dec)</p>
<p>    Client deposits		32,280.2 vs 32,440.3 (end Dec)</p>
<p>Note - Credito said it accounted for 3.48 percent of domestic bank deposits. It said the ratio of bad loans to all loans was 7.05 percent against a sector average of 10.35 percent. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
